Supreme People's Court

Notice on Issuing the Several Opinions on the Disclosure of the Execution Process by People's Courts

Fa Fa [2014] No. 18

To the high people's courts of all provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government; the Military Court of the People's Liberation Army; and the Production and Construction Corps Branch of the High People's Court of the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region:

To implement the principle of openness in enforcement, standardize the disclosure of the enforcement process by people's courts, further enhance the transparency of enforcement work, and promote the construction of an enforcement information disclosure platform, the Supreme People's Court has formulated the Several Opinions on the Disclosure of the Execution Process by People's Courts. This Opinion is hereby issued to you; please strengthen organizational leadership, adopt effective measures, and earnestly carry out the work of disclosing enforcement process information in accordance with the requirements of this Opinion.

September 3, 2014

Several Opinions on the Disclosure of the Execution Process by People's Courts

In order to implement the principle of openness in enforcement, standardize the disclosure of the enforcement process by people's courts, facilitate the timely understanding by parties of the progress of case enforcement, better safeguard the rights of parties and the public to be informed, to participate, to express themselves, and to supervise enforcement work, further enhance the transparency of enforcement work, promote fairness through openness, and establish public trust through fairness, these Opinions are formulated in accordance with the provisions of the Supreme People's Court's Several Provisions on the Openness of Enforcement by People's Courts (Fa Fa [2006] No. 35), the Supreme People's Court's Several Opinions on Promoting the Construction of the Three Major Platforms for Judicial Openness (Fa Fa [2013] No. 13), and other relevant provisions, taking into account the actual circumstances of enforcement work.

I. General Requirements

Article 1 The enforcement process information of people's courts shall be disclosed on the principle of openness, with non-disclosure as the exception. All enforcement processes and related information that should be or may be disclosed according to law shall be disclosed without exception, achieving full disclosure of the entire enforcement case handling process, full notification of milestones, full connection of procedures, and full online publication of documents, so as to provide parties and the public with comprehensive, diversified, and real-time enforcement disclosure services, and comprehensively promote transparent enforcement.

Article 2 The disclosure of the enforcement process by people's courts shall be based on the Internet portal websites (government affairs websites) of people's courts at all levels as the fundamental platform and main channel for disclosure, supplemented by other platforms or channels such as SMS, telephone voice systems, electronic bulletin boards and touch screens, mobile application clients, court microblogs, and court WeChat public accounts, to disclose the milestone information of enforcement case process, case progress status, and relevant materials to the parties and their agents ad litem, and to disclose public information related to court enforcement work, such as enforcement service information and enforcement announcement information, to the public.

People's courts at all levels shall establish a functional module for querying enforcement process information on the trial process information disclosure website under their portal website (government affairs website). The Supreme People's Court shall establish the "China Enforcement Information Disclosure Website" on its government affairs website, set up an entry point for the "China Trial Process Information Disclosure Website," and provide functions for querying enforcement case process information as well as links to the enforcement process information disclosure platforms of all people's courts nationwide. People's courts at all levels shall establish telephone voice systems and set up electronic touch screens in places such as case filing halls or petition reception areas for use by parties, their agents ad litem, and the public to consult relevant enforcement disclosure matters. Courts with the necessary conditions shall establish electronic bulletin boards, add the 12368 intelligent SMS service platform, court microblogs, and court WeChat public accounts in the construction of the enforcement command system, and other disclosure channels.

II. Channels and Content of Disclosure

Article 3 The following enforcement case information shall be disclosed to the parties and their agents ad litem:

(1) Case filing information such as the names of the parties, case number, cause of action, and date of filing;
(2) The names and office telephone numbers of the enforcement judge and the clerk;
(3) Information on enforcement measures taken, including information on the inquiry, seizure, freezing, deduction, and impoundment of the judgment debtor's property;
(4) Information on compulsory measures taken, including judicial detention, fines, summons by force, search, restrictions on exit, restrictions on high consumption, and inclusion in the list of dishonest judgment debtors;
(5) Information on the disposal of enforcement property, including information on entrusted appraisal, auction, sale, and debt satisfaction through property;
(6) Information on property distribution and receipt and payment of enforcement proceeds, including the property distribution plan, objections to the property distribution plan, amendments to the property distribution plan, entry of enforcement proceeds into the court's dedicated enforcement account, and transfer of enforcement proceeds;
(7) Information on suspension of enforcement, stay of enforcement, entrusted enforcement, designated enforcement, or elevation of enforcement;
(8) Information on enforcement settlement agreements;
(9) Information on the conclusion of enforcement implementation cases, including the date of enforcement conclusion, the status of recovery of the enforcement subject matter, the method of conclusion, and consultation with the judgment creditor regarding the conclusion of the current enforcement procedure;
(10) Information on the date of filing of cases concerning enforcement objections, enforcement reconsideration, objections by third parties, change and addition of enforcement parties, the names and office telephone numbers of the judge in charge of the case and other members of the collegial panel and the clerk, enforcement rulings, and the date of case conclusion;
(11) Information on the date of filing of cases concerning enforcement petitions, enforcement supervision, enforcement oversight, the names and office telephone numbers of the judge in charge of the case and other members of the collegial panel and the clerk, the opinion on case handling, and the date of case conclusion;
(12) Information on the time and place of enforcement hearings and inquiries;
(13) The enforcement period or review period of the case, and any changes such as deduction or extension of the enforcement period or review period;
(14) Materials such as the notice of acceptance of the enforcement case, notice of enforcement, notice of property declaration, notice of inquiry, notice of hearing, summons, records of inquiry, records of investigation and evidence collection, and records of enforcement hearings;
(15) Adjudicatory documents such as enforcement rulings and enforcement decisions;
(16) Service information such as the time of commencement of service, the time of completion of service, and the method of service for enforcement adjudicatory documents;
(17) Information on the publication of enforcement adjudicatory documents on the enforcement process information disclosure module of the enforcement court, the China Enforcement Information Disclosure Website, and the China Judgments Online Website, including the time of publication and the method of query;
(18) Other enforcement process information required to be disclosed by relevant laws or judicial interpretations.

Article 4 Courts with the necessary conditions shall make audio and video recordings when inquiring with parties, conducting enforcement hearings, and carrying out major enforcement activities. After the inquiry, hearing, or enforcement activity is concluded, such audio and video recordings shall be disclosed to the parties and their agents ad litem. Where parties and their agents ad litem apply for access to the audio and video recordings, the enforcement court shall, after verifying their identity information, promptly provide access.

Article 5 People's courts at all levels shall generate electronic case files for enforcement cases through online case handling. The principal electronic case file shall be disclosed to the parties and their agents ad litem. Where parties and their agents ad litem apply for access to the electronic case file, the enforcement court shall, after verifying their identity information, promptly provide access.

Article 6 For procedural enforcement documents other than enforcement rulings and enforcement decisions, people's courts at all levels shall provide electronic service to the parties and their agents ad litem through the enforcement process information disclosure module. Where parties and their agents ad litem agree to accept enforcement documents served by electronic means, they shall submit a signed or sealed confirmation at the time of case filing.

Article 7 People's courts at all levels shall disclose to the public through their Internet portal website (government affairs website) the following information concerning the court:

(1) Institutional information such as the court address, traffic map, contact information, jurisdiction, subordinate courts, internal departments and their functions, and complaint channels;
(2) Personnel information such as the names and positions of the members of the adjudication committee, and the judges and enforcement personnel;
(3) Information on the enforcement disclosure guide, such as the scope of disclosure and methods of query for enforcement processes, enforcement adjudicatory documents, and enforcement information;
(4) Information on the enforcement guide, such as the conditions for filing an enforcement case, enforcement procedures, sample enforcement documents such as the application for enforcement, fee standards, conditions and procedures for reduction, exemption, or deferral of enforcement fees, and risk tips for applying for compulsory enforcement;
(5) Hearing announcements, reward announcements, and auction announcements;
(6) Name lists such as the name list of selected agencies for appraisal, auction, and other social intermediary agencies.
(7) Judicial interpretations, guiding cases, and enforcement business documents.

III. Disclosure Process

Article 8 Except for cases concerning enforcement instructions and enforcement coordination, all types of enforcement cases accepted by people's courts at all levels shall promptly send automatic SMS notifications to the mobile phone numbers reserved by the parties and their agents ad litem, indicating the progress of the case process and reminding the parties and their agents ad litem to promptly accept enforcement documents served electronically.

When the case filing department or the enforcement agency serves the notice of acceptance of the enforcement case, the notice of enforcement, or other documents on the parties and their agents ad litem, it shall inform them of the methods for querying the progress of the case process and accepting electronic service of enforcement documents, and shall carry out publicity, consultation, and other related work.

During the enforcement proceedings, if a party or agent ad litem is added or changed, the enforcement agency shall inform the relevant person of the foregoing matters when serving the relevant legal documents.

Article 9 During the handling of an enforcement case, the parties and their agents ad litem may, using their valid identification number or organization code, mobile phone number, and the query code and password provided by the enforcement court, access and download relevant enforcement process information and materials through various media such as the enforcement process information disclosure module, telephone voice system, electronic bulletin boards and touch screens, mobile application clients, court microblogs, and court WeChat public accounts.

Article 10 The enforcement process information disclosure module shall have bidirectional interaction functionality. After logging into the enforcement process information disclosure module, the parties and their agents ad litem may leave messages for the judge handling the case. The content of such messages shall be automatically imported into the online case handling platform the following day, and the judge handling the case may reply to the messages through the online case handling platform.

Article 11 Parties and their agents ad litem who agree to accept enforcement documents served by electronic means may, through the enforcement process information disclosure module, acknowledge receipt of various enforcement documents served by the enforcement court by electronic means.

When a party or its agent ad litem downloads or accesses enforcement documents served by electronic means, a certificate of service shall be automatically generated, recording the name of the document downloaded by the person served, the time of download, the IP address, and other information. The automatically generated certificate of service shall be included in the electronic case file.

The clerk of the enforcement agency shall be responsible for tracking the acceptance of electronic service by the person served, and shall remind and guide the person served to promptly download and access enforcement documents served electronically. If the person served does not download or access the electronically served enforcement documents within three days after the sending of the reminder SMS, the documents shall be served by other means such as email, fax, or mail in a timely manner.

IV. Division of Duties and Responsibilities

Article 12 Courts with the capability to handle cases online shall strictly follow the relevant requirements for online case handling, circulate and approve enforcement cases within the online case handling system, produce various documents, records, and reports, and promptly, accurately, and completely scan and enter case materials and case information.

If an enforcement case, due to special circumstances, cannot be strictly handled online, the entry of case information shall be completed simultaneously with the actual operation.

If information cannot be entered in a timely manner due to special circumstances, the reasons shall be explained in detail and submitted to the head of the enforcement agency and the court leader in charge for approval.

Article 13 The enforcement process data generated by the online case handling system of people's courts at all levels and other process information generated during the enforcement process shall be stored in the database of the online case handling system as the basic data for enforcement information disclosure. Such data shall be synchronized to the enforcement information disclosure module on the Internet through data exchange, and the enforcement case process data shall be promptly, comprehensively, and accurately entered into the database of the national court enforcement case information management system.

The enforcement adjudicatory documents formed by the online case handling system of the enforcement court shall be exported, through data exchange, to the adjudicatory document disclosure website under the Internet portal website (government affairs website) of the enforcement court, and shall be provided with ports linking to the China Judgments Online Website and the China Enforcement Information Disclosure Website.

Article 14 If the judge handling the case considers that a specific case should not be fully or partially disclosed in accordance with Articles 3, 4, and 5 of these Opinions, the judge shall fill in the "Approval Form for Non-Disclosure of Enforcement Process Information," explain the reasons in detail, and after review by the head of the enforcement agency, submit it to the court leader in charge for approval.

Article 15 If information already published on the enforcement process information disclosure platform needs to be modified due to certain circumstances, the judge handling the case shall submit it to the leader of the enforcement agency for approval, promptly update the relevant information in the online case handling platform, and notify the parties and the network administrator, who shall promptly update the relevant information on the enforcement process information disclosure platform.

Article 16 The case filing departments and enforcement agencies of people's courts at all levels are the responsible departments for the disclosure of information on the progress of specific enforcement cases on the enforcement process information disclosure platform, and are responsible for ensuring the accuracy and completeness of case information and the timeliness of its entry and disclosure.

Article 17 The judicial administration and equipment management departments of people's courts at all levels shall provide material support for the enforcement information disclosure work.

The information technology department shall be responsible for website construction, operation and maintenance, and technical support, and shall supervise the relevant departments to export, on a daily and scheduled basis, the relevant information data in the online case handling platform, including various enforcement documents signed and issued by leaders, to the enforcement process information disclosure platform, and through the enforcement process information disclosure platform, import the collected relevant information, including automatically generated certificates of service, into the online case handling platform, so as to achieve secure data transmission and connection between the online case handling platform and the enforcement process information disclosure platform.

Article 18 The trial management department shall be responsible for organizing and implementing the enforcement process disclosure work, supervising the enforcement process information disclosure platform, conducting timely inspections, summarizing work information, reporting work status to the court leadership, issuing circulars, and carrying out supervision and urging.

If case information is found to be incomplete, belatedly disclosed, or erroneous, the trial management department shall urge the relevant departments to make corrections, and coordinate with and guide the information technology department to promptly update the information.

Article 19 The release and updating of information disclosed to the public shall be the responsibility of the specific department designated by each court.

V. Responsibilities and Evaluation

Article 20 If, due to negligence, significant errors or omissions occur in the disclosed enforcement process information, causing serious consequences, the relevant personnel shall be held accountable in accordance with relevant provisions.

Article 21 The disclosure of enforcement process information shall be included in the performance evaluation scope of judicial openness work. The specific evaluation methods shall be formulated separately.

VI. Supplementary Provisions

Article 22 These Opinions shall come into effect on the date of issuance.
